<section id="prevention"><h2>Fire Prevention</h2><ul><li>Minimize ignition sources near flammable materials.</li><li>Keep exits, aisles and extinguisher access clear.</li><li>Use approved containers and grounding where required.</li><li>Return gas cylinders to safe storage and keep incompatible materials separated.</li></ul></section>
<section id="classes"><h2>Fire Classes</h2><p>Class A: ordinary combustibles. Class B: flammable liquids and gases. Class C: energized electrical equipment. Class D: combustible metals. Class K: cooking oils and fats. Verify local classifications and approved equipment before response.</p></section>
<section id="response"><h2>Emergency Response</h2><ol><li>Raise the alarm and call emergency services.</li><li>Evacuate if fire, smoke or toxic gas threatens escape.</li><li>Attempt extinguisher use only after training, when the exit is safe behind you and the fire is incipient.</li><li>Never enter a smoke-filled or unknown-risk area.</li></ol></section>
<section id="extinguishers"><h2>Using an Extinguisher</h2><p>Use only the extinguisher type approved for the fuel and trained conditions. The PASS method means Pull, Aim, Squeeze and Sweep. Back away if fire grows or spreads.</p></section>
<section id="evacuation"><h2>Evacuation</h2><p>Follow marked exits without collecting personal belongings. Proceed to the designated assembly area, report missing persons and await official clearance before re-entry.</p></section>';
